OL,3,GNEWSA'Sinn Fein will not walk away from
OL,4,AStormont', says Michelle O'Neill
OL,5,
OL,6,FSinn Fein "is not walking away" from
OL,7,FStormont despite "the challenges of
OL,8,Fbeing in an executive with people who
OL,9,Fare fundamentally opposed to
OL,10,Fpower-sharing, to rights and equality",
OL,11,Fthe first minister has said.
OL,13,FMichelle O'Neill's comments came after
OL,14,Fspeculation her party could be
OL,15,Fconsidering it after Conor Murphy
OL,16,Fwarned there was "a danger the wheels
OL,17,Fcould come off" without institutional
OL,18,Freform.
OL,20,FThe party's deputy leader was speaking
OL,21,Fat a hunger strike commemoration in
OL,22,FBallina, County Mayo on Sunday.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,414,410,260,120,0,100
